Closes the java half of WI-nakut. Three commits: the producer fix, a linker
guard the measurement forced, and the measurement record.

## 1. The name slot of an unresolved java call names the CALLEE

java glued the receiver identifier into it — `java:external:0-0:u.mkdirs:unresolved`
rather than `mkdirs`, `out.println` rather than `println` — so every consumer that
asks a catalogue about a name got a string no catalogue has ever keyed.

**Parity, measured.** One fixture per language, same construct, through the shipped
survey: go `Write`, kotlin `write`, python `sendall`, rust `write_all`, scala
`write` — and java `u.write`. java was also inconsistent with itself: two of its five
emit branches already shortened, two left `strip_redundant_module_qualifier` to do it
downstream, and the placeholder case had nothing anywhere able to. The slot's content
was a function of which resolution branch fired.

**Two shipped disclosures were wrong.** The boundary-scoped `untyped_receiver` caveat
matches the callee name against method-kind catalogue rows, so it could never fire for
java — match-as-written is **0** on all three sizing repositories. And the unscoped
`unknown_receiver_scope` caveat prints a distinct-method COUNT that the receiver
spellings inflated **29% / 102% / 176%**: cassandra reported 22,584 distinct methods
where there are 8,191, with `get` alone printed as **427** separate "methods".

**No verdict can move**, and the guard is one the tree already argues: every edge this
shortens carries `call_construct="method"`, `gate_named_entry` refuses a
method-construct call with no module hint for every kind, and
`_register_sanitizer_callers` refuses on the same stamp. Both directions are pinned as
refutation cells.

**No capitalisation exemption, and that is measured.** Sparing `Foo.bar` on the theory
that it names a type was refuted on the data: jenkins' capitalised bucket is
SCREAMING_CASE static fields (`ALL.getName`, `CONFIG.getName`, `DESCRIPTOR.get`).

## 2. A class hint that contradicts the declared receiver type recovers nothing

Found by the measurement, not by reading. Java's variable-receiver calls reached the
`method-call-recovery` linker for the first time — it reads the id's name slot verbatim
— and it resolved them wrongly. On sherpa-onnx **all nine** newly-recovered rows are
`audio.getSampleRate()` resolved to `OfflineTts.getSampleRate`, where `audio` is a
`GeneratedAudio` that declares `getSampleRate` itself and six classes in the repository
declare it.

The evidence to refuse was already stamped: `receiver_type_hint` reads `GeneratedAudio`
on the wrong rows and `OfflineStream` / `AudioTagging` on the right ones. A contradicting
hint is now dropped from the candidate set. As wide as the evidence and no wider — an
edge with no stamp is unchanged, which is the WI-gigoz shape the linker was built for.

## 3. Measurement 0018

Three asserted arms by blob, two java repositories, plus a shipped-CLI fixture for the
one cell they cannot reach (every boundary claim on both is violated or inconclusive,
and a caveat attaches only on a clean path).

- **34 claim evaluations, zero verdicts moved**, in either direction; no other language moved.
- The scoped caveat now attributes **974 edges / 43 names / 9 boundaries** on jenkins over 650 already matching.
- End to end on the CLI: `distinct method(s): u.mkdirs` becomes a scoped caveat naming `fs_write` at `src/App.java:10 mkdirs()`.
- **A pre-registered clause was refuted and was the wrong test.** The guard removes 262 recoveries that predate this PR; a seeded sample of 12 is **12 of 12 false resolutions** (`map.put("A","a")` → `EnvVars.put` on a `TreeMap`, `w.flush()` → `AtomicFileWriter.flush` on a `PrintWriter`).

A cross-language parity gate pins the invariant for the next analyzer; verified
non-vacuous by restoring baseline `java.py`, where it fails for java alone.

26 existing assertions across three java test files are re-pointed and one test
re-titled. 10,807 tests pass, 100% coverage on changed files, ratchet clean.

